# SPA fallback + API exclusions. Order matters: first match wins.
# Keep this file plain ASCII - see docs/handoff/DEPLOY_NOTES_redirects.md.
#
# The target below is NOT named 404.html on purpose: Cloudflare Pages serves a
# file named 404.html for every unmatched path, before the /* rewrite below is
# applied - which silently killed every deep link on the site.
#
# Three graphql lines, not two: "/graphql/" with a trailing slash matches neither
# "/graphql" nor "/graphql/*" (the splat wants at least one character), so it fell
# through to the SPA rule and returned the app. Found live 16.08.
/graphql/*   /no-api.html   404
/graphql/    /no-api.html   404
/graphql     /no-api.html   404
/api/*       /no-api.html   404
/api/        /no-api.html   404
/api         /no-api.html   404
/*           /index.html    200
